    "# Part 2: Fit a Multiple Logistic-Regression Model\n",
    "\n",
    "## <img src=\"tutorial-icons/theory.png\" alt=\"Theory\" width=\"36\" style=\"vertical-align:middle; margin-right:9px;\"> Theory: Why the Fitting Code Has These Pieces\n",
    "\n",
    "| Code object or setting | Variables used here | Why it exists |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `X` | `GenderBinary`, `Age`, `EstimatedSalary` | Holds the predictors supplied to the model. |\n",
    "| `y` | `Purchased` | Holds the observed outcome group, coded 0 or 1. |\n",
    "| `X_train`, `y_train` | 80% of eligible rows | Fit preprocessing and logistic-regression coefficients. |\n",
    "| `X_test`, `y_test` | 20% of eligible rows | Provide one untouched final evaluation. |\n",
    "| `random_state=1099` | The row split | Makes the same rows enter each partition when the notebook is rerun. |\n",
    "| `stratify=y` | The two outcome groups | Keeps their proportions reasonably similar in the two row partitions. |\n",
    "| `StandardScaler` | `Age`, `EstimatedSalary` only | Centers each continuous predictor and divides by its training-set standard deviation so their different units do not dominate numerical optimization. |\n",
    "| `passthrough` | `GenderBinary` | Keeps the supplied 0/1 group indicator unchanged rather than treating it as a continuous measurement. |\n",
    "| `Pipeline` | Preprocessor + model | Learns every preprocessing step from training rows and reuses it consistently. |\n",
    "| `max_iter=2000` | Logistic optimizer | Sets a maximum number of optimization iterations. The model can stop sooner when it converges; the limit prevents endless fitting and can be raised if a convergence warning appears. |\n",
    "\n",
    "Standardization changes the units used by the fitting algorithm; it does not change which user belongs to an observed outcome or demographic group. Including `GenderBinary` allows the supplied group code to influence predicted purchase probabilities, so its effect and consequences require human scrutiny.\n",
    "\n",
    "## <img src=\"tutorial-icons/without_claude.png\" alt=\"Without Claude\" width=\"36\" style=\"vertical-align:middle; margin-right:9px;\"> Without Claude: What Must Be Coordinated?\n",
    "\n",
